    "outcome": "Haro breaks the wax seal and forces the crate open to inspect its contents, revealing what Wren has been carrying all this way.",
    "stance": "hope"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren says no and refuses to pay the additional two days, either confronting Haro about the discretionary charge or testing whether he can force his way past the gate.",
    "stance": "hope"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren pays Haro nine days' worth and proceeds through the Ferrous Gate with the sealed crate still intact, continuing down the road.",
    "stance": "neither"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro uses his gate-keys to break the wax seal and open the crate for inspection, exposing its contents to view.",
    "stance": "hope"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren refuses to pay the extra two days and attempts to carry the sealed crate around the Ferrous Gate, bypassing the toll station entirely.",
    "stance": "dread"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren refuses to pay nine days and steps toward the gate anyway. An invisible barrier, sudden weight, or System constraint stops him before he passes through the iron uprights.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren accepts the nine-day toll, marks the ledger, shoulders the frame, and walks through the gate onto the road beyond.",
    "stance": "neither"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro reveals something about the sealed crate—its sender, its contents, or why the wax cost extra—that reframes the nine-day toll as a rule rather than arbitrary extortion.",
    "stance": "hope"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Haro breaks the wax seal on the crate with a knife or tool, peeling it back to inspect the contents inside. Wren watches as the protective seal that kept the cargo intact is compromised.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren counts out whatever the nine days cost him—time from his indenture, or coin, or hours of labor—and hands it to Haro. The collector marks it in his ledger and allows Wren to reload the crate onto his frame.",
    "stance": "neither"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren lifts the crate back onto his shoulders, turns from the gate, and walks deliberately into the grass beside the road, attempting to bypass Haro's authority entirely and circumvent the toll.",
    "stance": "dread"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren accepts the revised toll of 9 days, shoulders the frame and crate again, and continues north past the gate—one more loss added to the ledger Haro keeps.",
    "stance": "neither"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren refuses to pay the extra two days. Haro calls out or signals, and armed gate-keepers emerge through the door to physically block him or seize the crate until the full toll is paid.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro breaks the wax seal and opens the crate. What is inside forces both men into something neither the gate's rules nor Wren's indenture were designed to handle.",
    "stance": "hope"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren pays Haro 9 days and crosses. On the far side, the lost time manifests—he's weaker, slower, or late to his delivery—and he faces a consequence he wasn't prepared for.",
    "stance": "neither"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren refuses and tries to walk around the gate. As he moves past the uprights, he hits a barrier or is stopped by guards. Haro watches without surprise.",
    "stance": "hope"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro's inspection breaks the seal. The crate holds something alive or magical that Wren was carrying blind, and Haro's recognition of it changes everything.",
    "stance": "dread"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren accepts the 9-day toll and passes through the gate with the sealed crate.",
    "stance": "neither"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren questions Haro about why the toll increased, or refuses to accept 9 days instead of the posted 7.",
    "stance": "hope"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro breaks the wax seal and opens the crate to inspect its contents.",
    "stance": "dread"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren pays the 9-day toll to Haro, the ledger is marked with another date, and he passes through the Ferrous Gate with the sealed crate on his back.",
    "stance": "neither"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro breaks the wax seal on the crate to properly inspect the contents, compromising the sealed condition that Wren was hired to protect.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren realizes he cannot pay 9 days and says so; Haro refuses to let him pass, leaving him trapped at the gate with no way forward.",
    "stance": "dread"
  }
]

