  {
    "outcome": "Wren pays the nine days in toll, hoists the sealed crate back onto his frame, and walks through the Ferrous Gate into the haze beyond.",
    "stance": "neither"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro, watching Wren pick up the crate, tells him something about the seal or the cargo that makes it clear the seal is containing something dangerous, and Wren realizes he has been carrying something far more significant than a simple delivery.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "As Wren moves past the gate, he sees the reason men who tried to walk around did not make it—marks or signs on the ground, or movement, or a warning carved into the stone—that tells him the gate is not the only obstacle on the road."
    ,
    "stance": "dread"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren produces payment for 9 days from his belongings and hands it to Haro, who marks it in the ledger with a steady hand; the collector steps aside and Wren hoists the empty-feeling frame back onto his shoulders to pass through the Ferrous Gate.",
    "stance": "neither"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro refuses to accept payment without breaking the wax seal to inspect the crate's contents; Wren realizes he has no recourse and watches as the collector opens what he's been carrying since the low bridges.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren glances at the two figures at the bottom of his ledger line and notices something has shifted—a number has moved in a direction that suggests his years of indenture may be nearing its end.",
    "stance": "hope"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Haro breaks the wax seal on the crate and inspects its contents at the Ferrous Gate. What's inside either justifies the 9-day surcharge or gives Wren grounds to refuse it.",
    "stance": "hope"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren pays the 9 days toll to Haro, who records the transaction in his ledger, and the moment passes without explanation or appeal.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren attempts to walk his crate around the Ferrous Gate rather than pay, and encounters whatever happened to the men who tried.",
    "stance": "hope"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren pays Haro the 9-day toll and continues through the gate with his empty frame.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro breaks the wax seal and opens the crate to examine its contents.",
    "stance": "neither"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren argues that the toll board posts 7 days and demands to know what authority permits Haro to add 2 more.",
    "stance": "hope"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren reaches for his ledger or pack to attempt payment of 9 days to Haro, revealing what the toll currency is and whether he can afford it.",
    "stance": "hope"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren steps past the white line and walks into the unmade land around the Ferrous Gate, discovering what stops the men who have tried to walk around.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro selects a key from his gate-ring and approaches the pale-wood crate to break its wax seal and inspect the contents directly.",
    "stance": "neither"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren pays Haro nine days—in tokens, marks, or debt-notation—and his entry in Haro's ledger is updated with the date and amount. Wren shoulders the crate and walks through the Ferrous Gate into whatever lies beyond.",
    "stance": "neither"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren refuses or turns to leave. When he tries to walk around the gate's iron uprights to avoid the toll, or backs away from it entirely, something stops him—a guard appears, an invisible boundary at the white line holds him, or the gate's structure itself prevents passage without payment.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro breaks the wax seal with one of his gate-keys and examines the crate's contents. He sees something that shifts his expression, then re-seals it and states a new assessment—either 'Nine days stands' or something that indicates he now understands why the cargo warranted the extra toll.",
    "stance": "neither"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren pays the nine days in whatever currency he carries, Haro stamps the ledger with a new line of dates and debts, and Wren lifts the crate back onto his frame to continue down the Road.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro tells Wren that sealed cargo carries additional inspection fees at the next gate, and warns him the toll will be higher there—information that suggests the crate's protection is itself a debt trap.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren reaches his destination, delivers the crate, and the recipient mentions they could buy out his indenture if he could be persuaded to stay—a conversation suggesting the system has an escape clause, though an expensive one.",
    "stance": "hope"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren surrenders 9 days to Haro and is permitted through the Ferrous Gate, his debt ledger updated and his burden unchanged.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro breaks the wax seal on the crate and forces Wren to reveal its contents, ending the mystery of what he's been carrying.",
    "stance": "hope"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren attempts to walk around the gate's iron uprights instead of passing through, testing whether the Road's system truly governs the entire path.",
    "stance": "dread"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren gives a gesture of acceptance or nods toward Haro. Haro marks the 9 days in the ledger, ink scratching on the page. Wren turns back to the crate to re-rope it for the next leg.",
    "stance": "neither"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro steps to the crate again and, with a gate-key or his bare hands, breaks the wax seal. The lid comes open. Haro's face changes at what he sees inside, though we—and Wren—cannot yet see it.",
    "stance": "hope"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren stares at his owed days in the ledger—4,027—and tells Haro he won't pay the nine. Haro sets the pen down very carefully. His voice gets quieter, not louder, and he mentions the Road.",
    "stance": "dread"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren admits he lacks 9 days to pay and Haro records the additional debt in his ledger, confirming that the System simply accrues the charge—Wren will owe more with each day that passes from here.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Before Wren speaks, Haro checks a second page in his ledger and says: 'Your patron paid through gate sixteen. This toll is covered.' Wren may take the crate across.",
    "stance": "hope"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren reaches for the crate to carry it around the gate's left upright instead of paying, and Haro says without looking up: 'That's not passage, Idren. The Road calls that refusal.' His hand moves to a different page.",
    "stance": "dread"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Haro breaks the wax seal on the crate to inspect its contents, revealing what's inside.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Unable to afford the nine-day toll, Wren walks around the gate rather than pay, incurring additional debt from the Road.",
    "stance": "neither"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro refuses passage until the toll is paid in full, leaving Wren trapped at the gate with the crate.",
    "stance": "dread"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Haro demands to break the wax seal and open the crate to verify the contents, citing \"subject to inspection\" as his authority. Wren must choose between violating the shipper's seal or refusing Haro and compounding his debt.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren agrees to pay the 9 days, and Haro explains that payment is immediate and automatic—time simply deducted from what Wren has left to live on the Road, added to his 4,027-day total. The weight settles deeper.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "The seal is deemed intact enough to pass. Wren shoulders the crate again and walks through the Ferrous Gate onto the road beyond with the cargo still sealed and uncompromised.",
    "stance": "hope"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren admits he cannot pay the 9 days. Haro tells him the Gate cannot be passed without settlement—he must either turn back down the Road or wait here.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Another traveler appears out of the haze approaching the Gate from the far side, and Haro's attention shifts to them, setting Wren's ledger aside momentarily.",
    "stance": "hope"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren asks what happens if he breaks the seal. Haro tells him the crate cannot be opened without paying a debt that exceeds his remaining life span.",
    "stance": "dread"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren shifts the frame back onto his shoulders and walks around the iron uprights of the Ferrous Gate to avoid paying the toll.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro uses a tool to break the wax seal and opens the crate, inspecting its sealed contents.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Another porter arrives at the Ferrous Gate from the opposite direction, carrying an empty frame.",
    "stance": "hope"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Wren pays the 9-day toll to Haro and crosses the Ferrous Gate, continuing down the road with the sealed crate. The ledger updates, his debt grows.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro breaks the wax seal on the crate as part of his inspection, opening it and revealing its contents to Wren.",
    "stance": "hope"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren refuses to pay the 9-day toll; Haro denies passage, and Wren is trapped at the gate, forced to choose between payment, walking around (incurring a worse debt per the Road's rules), or abandoning the crate.",
    "stance": "dread"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Haro breaks the wax seal and opens the crate, finding it contains something unexpected—either empty, or marked in a way that makes Haro recognize or hesitate.",
    "stance": "hope"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren pays the nine days without negotiating, shoulders the frame again, and passes through the gate to discover what lies beyond it: another toll, a settlement, or the destination this cargo was meant for.",
    "stance": "hope"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Wren asks Haro a direct question about his debt or attempts to understand how anyone escapes this arithmetic, and Haro either ignores him or reveals that the numbers work differently than Wren believes.",
    "stance": "neither"
  }
]

[
  {
    "outcome": "Haro marks the nine days in his ledger, nods Wren through, and Wren shoulders the crate again. He walks past the Ferrous Gate into whatever road lies beyond.",
    "stance": "neither"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "Haro or an authority from inside the gate demands the sealed crate be opened for inspection. Wren must choose whether to break the seal himself or stand and watch while someone else does.",
    "stance": "dread"
  },
  {
    "outcome": "A second figure emerges from the small door behind Haro—a gate-master or higher collector—and Haro defers to them. They examine the crate and the ledger, and impose an additional condition Wren did not expect.",
    "stance": "dread"
  }
